Cell["\<\
Currently we only compute the Incidence and Reflection amplitude for the In \
solution. The respective Up expressions are sparse in the literature. There \
is a preliminary version in the hidden Teukolsky`PN`Tools`, however it is \
slow and not thoroughly checked. We leave this work to a future release.  \
\>", "ExampleText",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947331922724276*^9, 3.947332037412699*^9}, {
  3.94733211327143*^9, 3.947332114529225*^9}, {3.94733217712227*^9, 
